  "configuration_id": "config_045",
  "reason": "The current best is config_024 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc=0.7250). All top-performing components have been identified: scvi_n200 >> pca_n2000 >> scgpt for RNA, imagenet_vit_l > resnet50 for image, transformer > avgpool for aggregation, and weighted ≥ concat for fusion. No untested configuration combines all best components in a new way, so beating 0.7250 is unlikely. However, config_045 (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) is the most informative remaining experiment: it tests whether the ~2% transformer-over-avgpool gain observed with scvi_n200 (0.7250 vs 0.7062) generalizes to pca_n2000, clarifying whether aggregation method interacts with RNA encoder quality. This completes a key cell in the encoder × aggregation grid and provides evidence for the final experiment's selection. Expected cost is moderate (~5–6 GPU hours), comparable to config_006 (7.02) but likely lower since transformer aggregation was cheaper than avgpool in prior runs (3.60 vs 4.82 for the scvi_n200/vit_l pair)."
}

